  "findings": [
    "Run91 Ubuntu26 passed the bubblewrap version and both Tesseract readiness stages, then Python could not open the fixed script with EPERM and exited2. No native denial case ran.",
    "The image-version-specific GitHub runner README identifies system Python3.14.4. The artifact does not hash or print the actual interpreter, so this identifies the image documentation, not an observed binary pin.",
    "CPython v3.14.4 main.c calls Py_fopen for the filename. Py_fopen calls set_inheritable with raise=1. Its Linux ioctl(FIOCLEX) fast path treats EPERM as an error instead of falling back to fcntl. Script-open failure is printed with exit2.",
    "The existing x86_64 policy denies every ioctl with EPERM and allows fcntl/openat. This source path can produce the observed error even if opening the bound script itself succeeds.",
    "CPython3.13.0 uses _Py_fopen_obj with the same set_inheritable path. This is not claimed to be a newly introduced Python3.14 behavior.",
    "AppArmor profile-file presence and parent label do not establish the child label or the denied syscall. There is no syscall trace or child-label evidence in this artifact."
  ],
